: \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 1385 to 1186 is supported by the temporal evidence in [61549,99948]. There are no direct events 1385->1186 (step_02), 1385's outgoing neighbors in the window do not include 1186 (step_01), and 1186's inbound neighbors do not include 1385 (step_04). k-hop static neighborhood checks around 1385 and 1186 (steps_03 and _06) do not reveal a static path that would enable a timely chain, and the obvious single-relay candidate 639 receives from 1385 (step_07) but shows no events to 1186 (step_08). Activity counts (steps_05 and _11) and 639's many contacts (steps_09,_10) show nodes are active (ruling out inactivity as the reason), so the lack of a temporal chain is not merely due to silence \u2014 the temporal connectivity required for a cascade is absent.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 53056, "total_output_tokens": 6697, "total_tokens": 59753, "total_latency_ms": 102091, "llm_calls": 12, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}